 :rule-sketch
 {:proposal "A separate correspondence table (e.g. holes/labs/M-wm-wiring/wm-term-fields.edn): {registry-symbol -> #{map-field}}, with per-entry provenance (declarer, date, code sha). Not in the registry (futon2 theory document, different lane rhythm) and not in the map box (a box does not know which registry symbols its fields witness); registry rows may point at it, as :preference-schedule already does informally via :live-status :map."
  :rule "Edge e with symbols S is :declared only if every s in S is covered by the correspondence of some crediting field in fields-by-var(e). A symbol with NO correspondence entry makes the edge :cannot-tell (loud table gap). Full correspondences with no matching field make a new honest class :does-not-carry. Identity declarations (tau:=beta) are explicit entries owned by the table, not by a name matcher. Record-grain entries (e.g. :construction-receipt for pi, :cascade-spec for C_tau's ingredients) must be allowed, or the rule manufactures false negatives on E, Pi and r."
  :failure-behaviour "The edge drops out of the :declared count NAMING the uncovered symbol; the acceptance count never again conflates 'some field crosses' with 'the term crosses'."
  :sketch-results {:pass [:R2->R3a :R3a->R7 :R5->R6 :R17->R6 :R6->R17 :R7->R3 :R14->R6-via-identity]
                   :mixed [:R6->R4-r-passes-pi-needs-record-grain-entry]
                   :exposed [:CTAU-TOKEN->R5 :R6->R16]}}
